    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "Show that the sum of three consecutive integers is divisible by 3.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "The sum is $3(n+1)$, a multiple of 3.\n\nWrite the integers as $n$, $n+1$ and $n+2$, then collect like terms.",
      "worked": "Let the integers be $n$, $n+1$ and $n+2$, where $n$ is an integer.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}n+(n+1)+(n+2)&=3n+3\\\\n+(n+1)+(n+2)&=3(n+1).\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $n+1$ is an integer, the sum is divisible by 3.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
